---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const pageTitle = "Windows & Natural Light Options | Appalachian Sheds Inc.";
const pageDescription = "Compare pine barn sash, aluminum single-hung, insulated vinyl and specialty transom windows, with detailed installed-price planning guides.";
---
<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
<Fragment set:html={"<section class=\"article-hero\"><div class=\"shell\"><div class=\"breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/options-upgrades/\">Options &amp; Upgrades</a> / Windows &amp; Natural Light Options</div><div class=\"eyebrow\">CUSTOMIZATION TOPIC 19 \u00b7 Openings &amp; Access</div><h1>Windows &amp; Natural Light Options</h1><p>Compare four window families, installed planning prices, architectural accents, light, airflow, and privacy.</p></div><section class=\"asi-cost-review\" id=\"option-planning-prices\"><h2>Option pricing &amp; budget planning</h2><p class=\"asi-cost-alert\"><strong>Research-stage planning references:</strong> The figures below come from historical ASI planning material or approved model siding formulas. Historical amounts have NOT been verified as current Appalachian Sheds selling prices. They are not quotes. Final prices and any credits for included standard features must appear in a written proposal.</p><table class=\"asi-cost-list\"><thead><tr><th>Option / scope</th><th>Planning figure</th><th>Basis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Additional aluminum single-hung window</td><td>$235\u2013$335</td><td>per window, legacy reference; scope not confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Vinyl insulated window</td><td>$395\u2013$495</td><td>per window, legacy reference; scope not confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Specialty transom window</td><td>$400\u2013$1,095+</td><td>planning amount, historical</td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"asi-cost-note\">Standard ASI building features remain included in the approved model price. Figures shown are for planning context only; these are not added to the online shed calculator. No site-specific price should be inferred from a price per linear or square foot.</p><a href=\"/options-gallery/\">Explore visual option comparisons</a></section></section><section aria-label=\"Historical window option pricing clarification\" class=\"asi-window-integrity-note\"><div class=\"shell\"><p><strong>Planning-price reference:</strong> The listed window and accent prices are reproduced from the original options source for review; they are not independently confirmed current ASI selling prices. Model-specific standard window packages, exact product sizes, included trim, availability and installation pricing are confirmed in the written proposal.</p></div></section><section aria-labelledby=\"asi-windows-final-title\" id=\"asi-windows-final\">\n<div class=\"awf-shell\">\n<header class=\"awf-head\">\n<p class=\"awf-kicker\">Options &amp; Upgrades \u00b7 Windows &amp; Natural Light</p>\n<h2 class=\"awf-title\" id=\"asi-windows-final-title\">Choose the Right Light, Airflow, Privacy &amp; Exterior Balance</h2>\n<p class=\"awf-subtitle\">Natural Light \u00b7 Ventilation \u00b7 View \u00b7 Privacy \u00b7 Wall Function</p>\n<p class=\"awf-lede\">The right windows do more than brighten a building. They influence ventilation, privacy, usable wall space, exterior proportion, weather protection and whether the finished structure feels like simple storage or a thoughtfully designed backyard room.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"awf-divider\"></div>\n</header>\n<nav aria-label=\"Window option categories\" class=\"awf-category-nav\">\n<a href=\"#asi-window-barn-sash\"><strong>Pine Barn Sash Windows</strong><span>Window Option 01</span></a>\n<a href=\"#asi-window-aluminum\"><strong>Aluminum Single-Hung Windows</strong><span>Window Option 02</span></a>\n<a href=\"#asi-window-vinyl\"><strong>Vinyl Insulated Windows</strong><span>Window Option 03</span></a>\n<a href=\"#asi-window-feature\"><strong>Feature Transoms &amp; Specialty Windows</strong><span>Window Option 04</span></a>\n</nav>\n<div class=\"awf-intro-grid\">\n<section class=\"awf-intro-card\">\n<h3>More Windows Is Not Automatically Better</h3>\n<p>The best window plan brings light where it helps, preserves privacy where it matters, protects useful wall space and makes the exterior elevation look intentional.</p>\n<p>A storage building, workshop, garden building, backyard office and studio all need different window logic.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"awf-intro-card\">\n<h3>Choose Windows Before Wall Framing</h3>\n<p>Window size and location affect rough openings, headers, siding layout, flashing, trim, shelving, workbenches, electrical planning, insulation and interior finishes.</p>\n<p>Late window changes can affect labor, materials, wall function and final pricing.</p>\n</section>\n</div>\n<div aria-label=\"Window planning sequence\" class=\"awf-sequence\">\n<div><b>1</b><strong>Intended Use</strong><span>Storage, office, studio, workshop, garden building or retreat.</span></div>\n<div><b>2</b><strong>Interior Layout</strong><span>Desk, bench, shelves, storage, seating and equipment.</span></div>\n<div><b>3</b><strong>Light &amp; Privacy</strong><span>Views, sightlines, glare, wall function and security.</span></div>\n<div><b>4</b><strong>Window System</strong><span>Family, size, operation, flashing, trim and final scope.</span></div>\n</div>\n<!-- OPTION 01 -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-window-barn-sash-title\" class=\"awf-option\" id=\"asi-window-barn-sash\">\n<div class=\"awf-option-head\">\n<div class=\"awf-option-copy\">\n<span class=\"awf-mini\">Window Option 01</span>\n<h3 id=\"asi-window-barn-sash-title\">Pine Barn Sash Windows with Grids</h3>\n<p>Pine barn sash windows provide the strongest vintage and Appalachian character in the window lineup. Their divided-lite proportions work especially well on cottage, garden, carriage and barn-inspired buildings where the window itself should contribute to the architecture.</p>\n<p>The tradeoff is maintenance. Wood barn sash requires appropriate paint, stain or sealing and periodic inspection to protect the wood and maintain the exterior finish.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-option-character\">\n<span class=\"awf-character-label\">Architectural Character</span>\n<h3>Vintage. Warm. Divided-Lite. Handcrafted.</h3>\n<p>Best when authentic character matters more than the lowest-maintenance path.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-two-grid\">\n<section class=\"awf-panel\">\n<h4>Best Uses</h4>\n<ul class=\"awf-list\">\n<li>Garden buildings and cottage-style sheds</li>\n<li>Barn-inspired and carriage-style structures</li>\n<li>Home-facing elevations where architectural detail matters</li>\n<li>Traditional workshops and hobby buildings</li>\n<li>Buildings using wood trim or other Appalachian-style details</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"awf-panel\">\n<h4>Planning Notes</h4>\n<ul class=\"awf-list\">\n<li>Coordinate muntin pattern, trim width and surrounding siding</li>\n<li>Use window size in proportion to the wall elevation</li>\n<li>Protect useful interior wall space for shelving and storage</li>\n<li>Plan exterior finish and maintenance responsibility</li>\n<li>Flash and trim the opening as part of the wall weather system</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"awf-barn-price-title\" class=\"awf-pricing\">\n<div class=\"awf-pricing-head\">\n<h4 id=\"awf-barn-price-title\">Pine Barn Sash Planning Prices</h4>\n<p>Installed planning prices preserved from the supplied Appalachian Sheds source.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"awf-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr><th scope=\"col\">Barn Sash Option</th><th scope=\"col\">Size</th><th scope=\"col\">Installed Planning Price</th><th scope=\"col\">Best For</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Small Pine Barn Sash with Grids</td><td>18\" \u00d7 27\"</td><td>$235</td><td>Small vintage elevations, garden sheds and traditional wall balance</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium Pine Barn Sash with Grids</td><td>24\" \u00d7 29\"</td><td>$295</td><td>Cottage buildings, workshops and balanced sidewall daylight</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Large Pine Barn Sash with Grids</td><td>31\" \u00d7 29\"</td><td>$335</td><td>Stronger vintage character and larger wall presence</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Custom Barn Sash with Grids</td><td>Varies</td><td>Inquire</td><td>Special proportions and model-specific layouts</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"awf-price-note\">Wood barn sash provides authentic character but is not the lowest-maintenance window path.</p>\n</section>\n<section aria-label=\"Pine Barn Sash \u2014 Visual Examples\" class=\"awf-photo-gallery\"><h4>Pine Barn Sash \u2014 Visual Examples</h4><p class=\"awf-photo-intro\">See traditional divided-lite wood window character and frame detailing.</p><div class=\"awf-photo-grid\"><figure class=\"awf-photo-card\"><img alt=\"Pine barn sash with divided-light character installed in a traditional wood-sided building.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/options/windows/pine-barn-sash-installed.jpg\"/><figcaption><strong>Pine Barn Sash \u2014 Installed Example</strong><p>Pine barn sash with divided-light character installed in a traditional wood-sided building.</p></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"awf-photo-card\"><img alt=\"Closer view of the wood frame and divided-light grid pattern.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/options/windows/pine-barn-sash-detail.jpg\"/><figcaption><strong>Pine Barn Sash \u2014 Detail</strong><p>Closer view of the wood frame and divided-light grid pattern.</p></figcaption></figure></div><p class=\"awf-photo-caveat\">Illustrative photographs of design characteristics, not individually verified examples of each priced size or an assertion of a completed Appalachian Sheds project. Confirm exact product, size, operation, glazing, and finish in the written proposal.</p></section></section>\n<!-- OPTION 02 -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-window-aluminum-title\" class=\"awf-option\" id=\"asi-window-aluminum\">\n<div class=\"awf-option-head\">\n<div class=\"awf-option-copy\">\n<span class=\"awf-mini\">Window Option 02</span>\n<h3 id=\"asi-window-aluminum-title\">Aluminum Single-Hung Windows with Screens</h3>\n<p>Aluminum single-hung windows are the practical everyday choice for storage buildings, workshops, hobby buildings and garden sheds. They provide useful daylight and operable airflow without requiring the finish maintenance associated with wood barn sash.</p>\n<p>The main planning issue is placement. A larger operable window may improve light and ventilation, but it also consumes wall space that might otherwise hold shelves, workbenches or equipment.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-option-character\">\n<span class=\"awf-character-label\">Functional Character</span>\n<h3>Practical. Operable. Screened. Low Maintenance.</h3>\n<p>The strongest general-purpose window family for storage, workshops and everyday shed use.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-two-grid\">\n<section class=\"awf-panel\">\n<h4>Best Uses</h4>\n<ul class=\"awf-list\">\n<li>Basic and premium storage buildings</li>\n<li>Workshops and hobby buildings</li>\n<li>Garden sheds requiring airflow</li>\n<li>General-purpose buildings where ventilation matters</li>\n<li>Buildings where low maintenance is preferred over wood character</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"awf-panel\">\n<h4>Planning Notes</h4>\n<ul class=\"awf-list\">\n<li>Coordinate location around shelving and workbenches</li>\n<li>Review privacy and what can be seen from outside</li>\n<li>Confirm screen and sash operation</li>\n<li>Size the rough opening and header before framing</li>\n<li>Integrate flashing and exterior trim with the siding system</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"awf-aluminum-price-title\" class=\"awf-pricing\">\n<div class=\"awf-pricing-head\">\n<h4 id=\"awf-aluminum-price-title\">Aluminum Window Planning Prices</h4>\n<p>Installed planning prices preserved from the supplied Appalachian Sheds source.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"awf-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr><th scope=\"col\">Aluminum Window Option</th><th scope=\"col\">Size</th><th scope=\"col\">Installed Planning Price</th><th scope=\"col\">Best For</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Standard Aluminum Single-Hung with Screen</td><td>18\" \u00d7 27\"</td><td>$225</td><td>Compact daylight and ventilation for storage and smaller buildings</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Medium Aluminum Single-Hung with Screen</td><td>24\" \u00d7 40\"</td><td>$300</td><td>Workshops, garden sheds and general-purpose buildings</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Large Aluminum Single-Hung with Screen</td><td>30\" \u00d7 40\"</td><td>$375</td><td>More daylight, ventilation and stronger exterior presence</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"awf-price-note\">Larger windows should be selected only where wall function, workbench placement and privacy allow them.</p>\n</section>\n<section aria-label=\"Aluminum Window \u2014 Visual Examples\" class=\"awf-photo-gallery\"><h4>Aluminum Window \u2014 Visual Examples</h4><p class=\"awf-photo-intro\">Compare exterior frame appearance and detail. Exact size, operating sash, and screens are specified separately.</p><div class=\"awf-photo-grid\"><figure class=\"awf-photo-card\"><img alt=\"Aluminum-framed window on a siding-clad exterior; illustrative appearance, not a dimension-specific product photograph.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/options/windows/aluminum-single-hung-installed.jpg\"/><figcaption><strong>Aluminum Window \u2014 Exterior Example</strong><p>Aluminum-framed window on a siding-clad exterior; illustrative appearance, not a dimension-specific product photograph.</p></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"awf-photo-card\"><img alt=\"Detail view of a dark-finish aluminum-framed window; verify exact operability and screen package in the written scope.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/options/windows/aluminum-single-hung-screen-detail.jpg\"/><figcaption><strong>Aluminum Window \u2014 Frame Detail</strong><p>Detail view of a dark-finish aluminum-framed window; verify exact operability and screen package in the written scope.</p></figcaption></figure></div><p class=\"awf-photo-caveat\">Illustrative photographs of design characteristics, not individually verified examples of each priced size or an assertion of a completed Appalachian Sheds project. Confirm exact product, size, operation, glazing, and finish in the written proposal.</p></section></section>\n<!-- OPTION 03 -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-window-vinyl-title\" class=\"awf-option\" id=\"asi-window-vinyl\">\n<div class=\"awf-option-head\">\n<div class=\"awf-option-copy\">\n<span class=\"awf-mini\">Window Option 03</span>\n<h3 id=\"asi-window-vinyl-title\">Vinyl Insulated Windows</h3>\n<p>Vinyl insulated windows are the comfort-focused window upgrade for backyard offices, studios, hobby rooms and other buildings intended for more frequent personal use. They combine insulated glazing, operable sash and lower-maintenance exterior materials with a more residential finished-space feel.</p>\n<p>They should be coordinated with insulation, interior finish, privacy, glare, desk or furniture placement and future heating or cooling plans.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-option-character\">\n<span class=\"awf-character-label\">Comfort Character</span>\n<h3>Insulated. Residential. Operable. Refined.</h3>\n<p>Best for occupied or comfort-focused buildings where daily use matters more than basic storage simplicity.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-two-grid\">\n<section class=\"awf-panel\">\n<h4>Best Uses</h4>\n<ul class=\"awf-list\">\n<li>Backyard offices</li>\n<li>Creative studios</li>\n<li>Hobby rooms</li>\n<li>Comfort-focused garden buildings</li>\n<li>Premium flex spaces and finished interiors</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"awf-panel\">\n<h4>Planning Notes</h4>\n<ul class=\"awf-list\">\n<li>Coordinate glazing with glare and solar exposure</li>\n<li>Plan privacy from neighboring properties and the street</li>\n<li>Keep desk, furniture and electrical layouts in mind</li>\n<li>Use compatible flashing and air-sealing details</li>\n<li>Confirm product availability before final framing</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"awf-vinyl-price-title\" class=\"awf-pricing\">\n<div class=\"awf-pricing-head\">\n<h4 id=\"awf-vinyl-price-title\">Vinyl Insulated Window Planning Prices</h4>\n<p>Installed planning prices preserved from the supplied Appalachian Sheds source.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"awf-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr><th scope=\"col\">Vinyl Window Option</th><th scope=\"col\">Size</th><th scope=\"col\">Installed Planning Price</th><th scope=\"col\">Best For</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Medium Vinyl Insulated Window</td><td>24\" \u00d7 36\"</td><td>$395</td><td>Comfort-focused buildings, offices and hobby rooms</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Large Vinyl Insulated Window</td><td>30\" \u00d7 36\"</td><td>$425</td><td>More daylight for offices and studios</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Wide Vinyl Insulated Window</td><td>36\" \u00d7 36\"</td><td>$495</td><td>Larger comfort-focused wall openings in premium spaces</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"awf-price-note\">Insulated windows support comfort, but the building's full insulation, air-sealing and climate-control strategy remains a separate system.</p>\n</section>\n<section aria-label=\"Vinyl Insulated Window \u2014 Visual Examples\" class=\"awf-photo-gallery\"><h4>Vinyl Insulated Window \u2014 Visual Examples</h4><p class=\"awf-photo-intro\">See residential-style frame and trim treatments. Confirm the specified glazing and frame profile for your building.</p><div class=\"awf-photo-grid\"><figure class=\"awf-photo-card\"><img alt=\"White-framed residential-style window on a backyard building with cedar trim.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/options/windows/vinyl-insulated-installed.png\"/><figcaption><strong>Vinyl Insulated Window \u2014 Installed Example</strong><p>White-framed residential-style window on a backyard building with cedar trim.</p></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"awf-photo-card\"><img alt=\"Close-up of a window frame and sill showing installed exterior detailing.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/options/windows/vinyl-window-frame-detail.jpg\"/><figcaption><strong>Vinyl Window \u2014 Frame Detail</strong><p>Close-up of a window frame and sill showing installed exterior detailing.</p></figcaption></figure></div><p class=\"awf-photo-caveat\">Illustrative photographs of design characteristics, not individually verified examples of each priced size or an assertion of a completed Appalachian Sheds project. Confirm exact product, size, operation, glazing, and finish in the written proposal.</p></section></section>\n<!-- OPTION 04 -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-window-feature-title\" class=\"awf-option\" id=\"asi-window-feature\">\n<div class=\"awf-option-head\">\n<div class=\"awf-option-copy\">\n<span class=\"awf-mini\">Window Option 04</span>\n<h3 id=\"asi-window-feature-title\">Feature Transoms &amp; Specialty Windows</h3>\n<p>Feature transoms and specialty windows add light higher on the wall, helping preserve privacy and lower-wall function. They are especially useful on studios, offices, poolside buildings, feature walls and buildings where traditional low windows would interfere with storage, furniture or sightlines.</p>\n<p>This category also includes custom window sizes and specialty glazing directions that require early coordination with framing, trim and the overall elevation.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-option-character\">\n<span class=\"awf-character-label\">Architectural Character</span>\n<h3>High Light. Privacy. Feature Detail. Custom.</h3>\n<p>Best when the building needs more daylight without sacrificing as much privacy or usable lower-wall space.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-two-grid\">\n<section class=\"awf-panel\">\n<h4>Best Uses</h4>\n<ul class=\"awf-list\">\n<li>Studios and backyard offices</li>\n<li>Poolside buildings and changing areas</li>\n<li>Garden buildings and feature elevations</li>\n<li>Privacy-conscious walls</li>\n<li>Custom specialty buildings requiring unique proportions</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"awf-panel\">\n<h4>Planning Notes</h4>\n<ul class=\"awf-list\">\n<li>Coordinate length and height before wall framing</li>\n<li>Review header requirements and wall proportions</li>\n<li>Use high placement to protect privacy and lower-wall use</li>\n<li>Coordinate specialty glazing with lead time and supplier availability</li>\n<li>Integrate trim and flashing with the siding system</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"awf-feature-price-title\" class=\"awf-pricing\">\n<div class=\"awf-pricing-head\">\n<h4 id=\"awf-feature-price-title\">Feature &amp; Specialty Window Planning Prices</h4>\n<p>Planning ranges preserved from the supplied Appalachian Sheds source.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"awf-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr><th scope=\"col\">Feature Window Option</th><th scope=\"col\">Planning Price</th><th scope=\"col\">Best For</th><th scope=\"col\">Planning Note</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>5-Foot Transom Window Direction</td><td>$400\u2013$850+</td><td>Studios, offices, poolside rooms and privacy-conscious walls</td><td>Useful when daylight should sit higher on the wall</td></tr>\n<tr><td>6-Foot Transom Window Direction</td><td>$500\u2013$1,095+</td><td>Wider elevations, studios and feature walls</td><td>Requires early framing and trim coordination</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Bar-Window / Countertop Opening Direction</td><td>$700\u2013$1,095+</td><td>Entertaining sheds, poolside buildings and concession-style use</td><td>Requires counter, sill, weather and security review</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Insulated Transom or Specialty Window Package</td><td>Inquire</td><td>Custom comfort, appearance or performance needs</td><td>Price depends on glass, size, operation and installation details</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"awf-price-note\">Door glass remains coordinated with the Doors &amp; Entry Systems category rather than being treated as a separate window family here.</p>\n</section>\n<section aria-label=\"Transoms, Privacy Glass &amp; Entry Glass \u2014 Visual Examples\" class=\"awf-photo-gallery\"><h4>Transoms, Privacy Glass &amp; Entry Glass \u2014 Visual Examples</h4><p class=\"awf-photo-intro\">These images illustrate three different ways to use glass for high-level light, privacy, and a coordinated doorway.</p><div class=\"awf-photo-grid\"><figure class=\"awf-photo-card\"><img alt=\"Horizontal transom windows positioned high in a building wall above a door opening.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/options/windows/transom-installed.jpg\"/><figcaption><strong>High Transom Window \u2014 Example</strong><p>Horizontal transom windows positioned high in a building wall above a door opening.</p></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"awf-photo-card\"><img alt=\"Window with obscured glass allowing daylight while reducing direct visibility.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/options/windows/privacy-glazing-installed.jpg\"/><figcaption><strong>Privacy Glazing \u2014 Example</strong><p>Window with obscured glass allowing daylight while reducing direct visibility.</p></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"awf-photo-card\"><img alt=\"Glazed entry door example; door configuration belongs to the separate Door &amp; Entry Options category.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/options/windows/entry-door-glass.jpg\"/><figcaption><strong>Door Glass \u2014 Coordinated Entry Example</strong><p>Glazed entry door example; door configuration belongs to the separate Door &amp; Entry Options category.</p></figcaption></figure></div><p class=\"awf-photo-caveat\">Illustrative photographs of design characteristics, not individually verified examples of each priced size or an assertion of a completed Appalachian Sheds project. Confirm exact product, size, operation, glazing, and finish in the written proposal.</p></section></section>\n<!-- SUPPORTING ACCENTS -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"awf-accents-title\" class=\"awf-accents\">\n<div class=\"awf-section-head\">\n<span>Supporting Window Accents</span>\n<h3 id=\"awf-accents-title\">Trim &amp; Flower Boxes Finish the Opening \u2014 They Do Not Create the Window System</h3>\n<p>These are supporting exterior details rather than primary window families. They work best when used selectively on visible elevations.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-accent-grid\">\n<div class=\"awf-accent-card\"><strong>1 \u00d7 3 Trim \u2014 Standard Window</strong><span>$50 per window. Sharpens standard openings and improves exterior finish.</span></div>\n<div class=\"awf-accent-card\"><strong>1 \u00d7 3 Trim \u2014 Larger Window</strong><span>$75 per window. Helps larger openings look integrated with the elevation.</span></div>\n<div class=\"awf-accent-card\"><strong>Standard Flower Box</strong><span>$75 each. Best on garden, cottage and home-facing elevations.</span></div>\n<div class=\"awf-accent-card\"><strong>Large Flower Box</strong><span>$105 each. Proportional accent for larger windows; requires finish maintenance.</span></div>\n</div>\n<section aria-label=\"Flower Boxes \u2014 Visual Example\" class=\"awf-photo-gallery\"><h4>Flower Boxes \u2014 Visual Example</h4><p class=\"awf-photo-intro\">A decorative treatment that complements selected traditional window elevations.</p><div class=\"awf-photo-grid\"><figure class=\"awf-photo-card\"><img alt=\"Wood window with decorative flower box and planting beneath the sill.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/options/windows/flower-box-window-accent.jpg\"/><figcaption><strong>Window Flower Box \u2014 Accent Example</strong><p>Wood window with decorative flower box and planting beneath the sill.</p></figcaption></figure></div><p class=\"awf-photo-caveat\">Illustrative photographs of design characteristics, not individually verified examples of each priced size or an assertion of a completed Appalachian Sheds project. Confirm exact product, size, operation, glazing, and finish in the written proposal.</p></section></section>\n<!-- LIGHT / PRIVACY / WALL FUNCTION -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"awf-balance-title\" class=\"awf-balance\">\n<div class=\"awf-section-head\">\n<span>Light, Privacy &amp; Wall Function</span>\n<h3 id=\"awf-balance-title\">More Glass Is Not Always Better</h3>\n<p>Every opening adds light, but every opening also changes privacy, wall storage, glare, security and exterior rhythm.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-balance-grid\">\n<div class=\"awf-balance-card\"><strong>Natural Light</strong><p>Well-placed windows can make a small building feel larger and more comfortable.</p></div>\n<div class=\"awf-balance-card\"><strong>Ventilation</strong><p>Operable windows support airflow, but overall ventilation still depends on the complete building system.</p></div>\n<div class=\"awf-balance-card\"><strong>Privacy</strong><p>High windows and transoms can bring in light while reducing direct sightlines.</p></div>\n<div class=\"awf-balance-card\"><strong>Wall Function</strong><p>Every window reduces space available for shelves, benches, cabinets and equipment.</p></div>\n<div class=\"awf-balance-card\"><strong>Security</strong><p>Window height and glass area affect what can be seen from outside.</p></div>\n<div class=\"awf-balance-card\"><strong>View</strong><p>A carefully placed view window can make a workspace or retreat significantly more inviting.</p></div>\n<div class=\"awf-balance-card\"><strong>Glare</strong><p>South- and west-facing windows may create glare or added heat gain if not planned carefully.</p></div>\n<div class=\"awf-balance-card\"><strong>Exterior Rhythm</strong><p>Window size and spacing should support the siding, doors, roofline and trim package.</p></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<!-- COMPARISON -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"awf-compare-title\" class=\"awf-compare\">\n<div class=\"awf-compare-head\">\n<span>Final Window Comparison</span>\n<h3 id=\"awf-compare-title\">Four Window Families \u2014 Four Different Priorities</h3>\n<p>On smaller screens, swipe or scroll horizontally to see the complete comparison.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"awf-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Window Family</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Primary Strength</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Light / Airflow</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Maintenance</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Best Uses</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Planning Range</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Pine Barn Sash with Grids</td>\n<td>Strongest vintage / Appalachian character</td>\n<td>Good natural light; source emphasizes divided-lite character</td>\n<td>Highest finish-maintenance responsibility</td>\n<td>Garden, cottage, barn and carriage-style buildings</td>\n<td>$235\u2013$335 per window</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Aluminum Single-Hung with Screens</td>\n<td>Practical daylight and ventilation</td>\n<td>Operable sash and screens provide useful airflow</td>\n<td>Lower maintenance than wood</td>\n<td>Storage, workshops, hobby and general-purpose buildings</td>\n<td>$225\u2013$375 per window</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vinyl Insulated Windows</td>\n<td>Comfort-focused upgrade</td>\n<td>Insulated glazing, operable sash and screens</td>\n<td>Lower maintenance than wood</td>\n<td>Offices, studios, hobby rooms and comfort-focused buildings</td>\n<td>$395\u2013$495 per window</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Feature Transoms &amp; Specialty Windows</td>\n<td>Architectural light with better privacy / wall preservation</td>\n<td>High-level light; operation varies by selected product</td>\n<td>Depends on material and glazing</td>\n<td>Studios, offices, poolside rooms and feature elevations</td>\n<td>$400\u2013$1,095+ planning</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"awf-compare-note\">Window sizes, materials, glass, screens, operation, trim, finish requirements and availability vary by building model and current product availability. Final specifications and pricing are confirmed in the written project scope.</p>\n</section>\n<!-- WEATHER -->\n<section class=\"awf-weather\">\n<h3>Windows Are Weather Openings First and Design Features Second</h3>\n<p>Window performance depends on the opening around it. Sill or pan flashing, head flashing, jamb sealing, compatible air-sealing materials, trim and siding transitions all need to work together to manage water and air.</p>\n<p>Caulk at approved joints helps protect selected trim connections, but it does not replace proper flashing or drainage. Exterior finish, screens, glass, trim and sealants should also be inspected over time.</p>\n</section>\n<!-- CTA -->\n<section class=\"awf-cta\">\n<div class=\"awf-cta-copy\">\n<span>Choose Placement Before Quantity</span>\n<h3>Use the Fewest Windows That Fully Support the Building's Real Use</h3>\n<p>The best window plan balances light, airflow, privacy, view, wall function, weather detailing and exterior proportion without adding unnecessary openings.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"awf-cta-side\">\n<a href=\"/options-upgrades/\">Explore Options &amp; Upgrades</a>\n<a class=\"awf-ghost\" href=\"tel:15133792421\">Call Edwin \u00b7 (513) 379-2421</a>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</section>"} />
</Base>

